{# Conventional Commits format template #}
{# description: Generates commit messages following Conventional Commits specification #}
{# variables: changes, repository, user #}

{%- macro get_change_type(changes) -%}
{%- if changes.is_feature %}feat{% elif changes.is_fix %}fix{% elif changes.is_refactor %}refactor{% elif changes.is_docs %}docs{% elif changes.is_test %}test{% else %}chore{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro format_unified_diff(file) -%}
{%- if file.hunks %}
{%- for hunk in file.hunks[:5] %}
{%- if hunk.function_context %}
--- in {{ hunk.function_context }} ---
{%- endif %}
```diff
{%- for line in hunk.unified_lines[:15] %}
{{ line[:150] }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if hunk.unified_lines|length > 15 %}
  ... ({{ hunk.unified_lines|length - 15 }} more lines)
{%- endif %}
```
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif file.content_preview %}
```diff
{{ file.content_preview }}
```
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

Generate a commit message for the following changes:

## Summary
- Files changed: {{ changes.affected_files|length }}
- Lines added: +{{ changes.lines_added }}
- Lines removed: -{{ changes.lines_deleted }}
- Suggested type: {{ get_change_type(changes) }}
{%- if changes.scope %}
- Scope: {{ changes.scope }}
{%- endif %}

## Changed Files
{% for file in changes.affected_files %}
### {{ file.path }} ({{ file.change_type }}, +{{ file.lines_added }}/-{{ file.lines_deleted }})
{%- if file.is_test %} [TEST]{% endif %}
{%- if file.is_config %} [CONFIG]{% endif %}
{%- if file.is_docs %} [DOCS]{% endif %}

{{ format_unified_diff(file) }}
{% endfor %}

## Instructions
Analyze the unified diff above. Write a commit message:
1. Subject: type(scope): specific description naming the concrete code entity or behavior changed
2. Scope = module or component name from directory/class, NOT a file extension
3. Be precise: name functions, classes, config keys, endpoints, or values that changed
4. Body ONLY if change spans multiple concerns - explain WHY, not WHAT. Otherwise omit body entirely.
5. Do NOT restate the subject in the body. Do NOT start with "This commit" or "The changes".

Output ONLY the commit message.
